{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc | sed -n '1,230p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.jing.content.step\n     2\t  \"The stepped client half of the content service (docs/design/\n     3\t   dao.stream.remote.md section 5, the Linda request medium;\n     4\t   dao.jing.content holds the vocabulary). The portable interface, per\n     5\t   dao.stream.md OD-5: a pure client the caller steps, with the\n     6\t   request-put / request-get / request-materialize / step / abandon\n     7\t   shape the deleted dao.jing.remote.step carried, over a requests\n     8\t   writer and an answers reader that are reflections or local handles.\n     9\t\n    10\t   Everything here is a pure function over explicit data. No socket,\n    11\t   atom, promise, callback, or scheduler. The caller owns the state,\n    12\t   attaches it to whatever pair it has, and chooses every cadence.\n    13\t\n    14\t   The state is {:requests w :answers r :cursor c :unsent u\n    15\t   :outstanding {s request} :completed [...] :diagnostics [...]\n    16\t   :terminal nil :materializations {put-id record} :routes {live-id\n    17\t   put-id}}. A cursor is either one the answers reader handed out or an\n    18\t   anchor keyword -- :dao.stream/newest, the Linda mint -- which the\n    19\t   first poll resolves through the reader, retrying while the reader\n    20\t   answers a retryable mint (a reflection's cursor ask). A materialization\n    21\t   record is {:phase :put|:verify-unissued|:verify-issued :address a\n    22\t   :put-id s :get-id m?} -- an address, never a payload: nothing this\n    23\t   layer retains or publishes carries a payload. :routes maps every\n    24\t   answer id a record currently claims to the record's put id, which is\n    25\t   the identity a materialization's one published completion carries.\n    26\t\n    27\t   step advances in one fixed order, and the order is load-bearing:\n    28\t\n    29\t   1. re-append the retained :unsent request (a writer that answered\n    30\t      full), folding the outcome under :attempt;\n    31\t   2. poll at most `budget` answers, correlating each by :jing/request,\n    32\t      filing unknown or malformed values as diagnostics;\n    33\t   3. on a terminal reader, lose the retained request with the terminal\n    34\t      reason, so its loss surfaces on the ordinary completion path;\n    35\t   4. issue the unissued verify reads of :verify-unissued records, in\n    36\t      the order their puts were issued, until the writer answers full\n    37\t      or the reader ends;\n    38\t   5. route every completion: a found get answer and a :present verify\n    39\t      pass through the one ingress check dao.jing/accept-bytes! before\n    40\t      any value is published.\n    41\t\n    42\t   The verify hop is the one obligation the client carries for\n    43\t   materialization: a put answering :present has promised that equal\n    44\t   content sits at the address, and a remote server is not trusted to\n    45\t   have kept that promise. So :present publishes nothing; the record\n    46\t   moves to :verify-unissued, a correlated read is issued by order 4,\n    47\t   and only a read-back that verifies against the address completes\n    48\t   :result :present. The record's removal is the exactly-once guard:\n    49\t   one completion per materialization, carrying the put id.\n    50\t\n    51\t   Reattachment stays the caller's: after a terminal reason every\n    52\t   further request answers :terminal, and a new pair is a new client.\n    53\t   abandon retires only the retained :unsent request -- the one delivery\n    54\t   this binding still owes.\"\n    55\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n    56\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    57\t            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t;; =============================================================================\n    61\t;; Vocabulary\n    62\t;; =============================================================================\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(def get-op\n    66\t  \"The read operation this client speaks.\"\n    67\t  :jing/get)\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(def put-op\n    71\t  \"The write operation this client speaks.\"\n    72\t  :jing/put)\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(def malformed-response-code\n    76\t  \"The error code for an answer that does not conform to its request's\n    77\t   wire vocabulary -- a get not answering the exact found?/bytes shape,\n    78\t   a put not answering :inserted or :present.\"\n    79\t  :dao.jing.content/malformed-response)\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(def integrity-failure-code\n    83\t  \"The error code for content that fails the ingress check on arrival:\n    84\t   a found read-back that does not hash to the address it was read from,\n    85\t   or bytes that are not one canonical payload.\"\n    86\t  :dao.jing.content/integrity-failure)\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(def present-but-absent-code\n    90\t  \"The error code for a put that answered :present and a verify read\n    91\t   that then found nothing at the address.\"\n    92\t  :dao.jing.content/present-but-absent)\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(def abandoned-code\n    96\t  \"The default abandon reason: this layer's own word for a request given\n    97\t   up by policy rather than lost by the medium.\"\n    98\t  :dao.jing.content/abandoned)\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\t(def ^:private integrity-failure\n   102\t  \"The error map a failed ingress check publishes, by code.\"\n   103\t  {:code integrity-failure-code\n   104\t   :message \"the remote content does not hash to its content address\"})\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(def ^:private malformed-response\n   108\t  \"The error map for an answer outside its request's vocabulary.\"\n   109\t  {:code malformed-response-code\n   110\t   :message \"the answer does not conform to the request's vocabulary\"})\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(def ^:private present-but-absent\n   114\t  {:code present-but-absent-code\n   115\t   :message \"the remote reported :present but the content address is absent\"})\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- mint-id\n   119\t  \"A self-minted random request id, unique against this client's live\n   120\t   ids so callers sharing one answers stream do not collide.\"\n   121\t  [state]\n   122\t  (loop []\n   123\t    (let [id (str (random-uuid))]\n   124\t      (if (or (contains? (:outstanding state) id)\n   125\t              (= id (get-in state [:unsent :id])))\n   126\t        (recur)\n   127\t        id))))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- answer?\n   131\t  \"True for any well-formed answer value: the request id key, whatever\n   132\t   body follows it.\"\n   133\t  [v]\n   134\t  (and (map? v) (contains? v :jing/request)))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; State\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn client-state\n   143\t  \"The stepped client's state over one content pair: `requests` the\n   144\t   writer the client appends its requests to, `answers` the reader it\n   145\t   polls, `cursor` either a cursor `answers` handed out or an anchor\n   146\t   keyword (:dao.stream/newest, the Linda mint, resolved on the first\n   147\t   poll -- a reflection's mint is answered across the channel, so the\n   148\t   first steps may retry it). The caller owns the result and every step\n   149\t   of it.\"\n   150\t  [requests answers cursor]\n   151\t  {:requests requests\n   152\t   :answers answers\n   153\t   :cursor cursor\n   154\t   :unsent nil\n   155\t   :outstanding {}\n   156\t   :completed []\n   157\t   :diagnostics []\n   158\t   :terminal nil\n   159\t   :next-seq 0\n   160\t   :materializations {}\n   161\t   :routes {}})\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn- segment-address!\n   165\t  \"Throw unless `address` is a segment address: arbitrary keys and\n   166\t   mutable roots are refused before the wire.\"\n   167\t  [address]\n   168\t  (when-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n   169\t    (throw (ex-info \"a stepped content request names a non-segment address\"\n   170\t                    {:address address}))))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t(defn- register\n   174\t  \"Claim `id` for a materialization: the record (carrying its issue\n   175\t   order under :seq -- the ids are random, so the order the verify reads\n   176\t   issue in is the record's own) and its route.\"\n   177\t  [state id address]\n   178\t  (-> state\n   179\t      (assoc-in [:materializations id]\n   180\t                {:phase :put, :address address, :put-id id\n   181\t                 :seq (:next-seq state)})\n   182\t      (update :next-seq (fnil inc 0))\n   183\t      (assoc-in [:routes id] id)))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn- submit\n   187\t  \"The shared body of the request entry points: answer :terminal on a\n   188\t   client whose answers reader has ended (a new pair is a new client),\n   189\t   refuse with :busy while an unsent request is owed (only step's order\n   190\t   1 clears it), append the request value, and register a\n   191\t   materialization record at any id the writer's answer carries. A\n   192\t   writer refusal completes at once -- the record routes that loss at\n   193\t   the next drain.\"\n   194\t  [state request materialize?]\n   195\t  (cond\n   196\t    (:terminal state)\n   197\t    {:outcome :terminal, :state state}\n   198\t\n   199\t    (:unsent state)\n   200\t    {:outcome :busy, :state state}\n   201\t\n   202\t    :else\n   203\t    (let [id (mint-id state)\n   204\t          value (assoc request :jing/request id)\n   205\t          result (stream/append! (:requests state) value)\n   206\t          outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   207\t          address (get request put-op)]\n   208\t      (cond\n   209\t        (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   210\t        {:outcome :requested\n   211\t         :state (-> (assoc-in state [:outstanding id] request)\n   212\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   213\t         :id id}\n   214\t\n   215\t        (= :dao.stream/full outcome)\n   216\t        {:outcome :pending-request\n   217\t         :state (-> (assoc state :unsent {:id id, :value value})\n   218\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   219\t         :id id}\n   220\t\n   221\t        :else\n   222\t        ;; closed, invalid-value, transport-error: the append never\n   223\t        ;; happened; the loss completes on the ordinary path\n   224\t        {:outcome :request-undeliverable\n   225\t         :state (-> (update state :completed\n   226\t                            conj {:id id, :request request, :lost outcome})\n   227\t                    (cond-> materialize? (register id address)))\n   228\t         :id id\n   229\t         :reason outcome}))))\n   230\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
