{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md | sed -n '345,380p'\"","aggregated_output":"   345\tDirection is establishment, not authority. A WebSocket has a dialer and an\n   346\tacceptor because TCP does. Once established the channel is symmetric and\n   347\tnothing in this document remembers who dialed. Hosts: clj, cljs on Node and\n   348\tcljd may dial or accept (`src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj`,\n   349\t`src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/node.cljs`, `src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd`);\n   350\tcljs in a browser may only dial (`src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/browser.cljs`).\n   351\t\n   352\t### 3.2 UDP\n   353\t\n   354\t`dao.stream.udp` is a new channel with the WebSocket deposit model: a socket\n   355\tretains nothing, so it has no reader surface, and its adapter deposits every\n   356\tdatagram as an event carrying the datagram's source address and its decoded\n   357\tvalue onto the medium the composition wired. The socket itself, as raw\n   358\taddressed datagrams, is the layer beneath this channel:\n   359\t[`dao.stream.datagram.md`](./dao.stream.datagram.md), whose section 7 says how\n   360\tthis channel is fed from it and whose `bind-host`/`bind-port` descriptor keys\n   361\tname the local socket, not the destination named here.\n   362\t\n   363\t- Descriptor: `{:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/udp :dao.stream/identity\n   364\t  <channel identity> :dao.stream.udp/host h :dao.stream.udp/port p}`.\n   365\t  `attach!` binds or reuses a local socket and returns a handle whose writer\n   366\t  path is datagrams to that address.\n   367\t- One CBOR value per datagram, canonical profile. The budget covers the\n   368\t  whole encoded datagram, fragment envelope included: at most 1200 bytes,\n   369\t  the figure `dao.jing.dht.node` already uses to clear common path MTUs.\n   370\t- **Fragmentation is channel-internal.** An encoded message over budget is\n   371\t  split into `k` datagrams, each\n   372\t  `{:dao.stream.remote/id n :dao.stream.udp/part i :dao.stream.udp/parts k\n   373\t  :dao.stream.udp/bytes b}`, where `n` is the carried message's own request\n   374\t  id. The receiver reassembles by `[channel attachment identity,\n   375\t  source-address, direction, id]`, because ids are unique only per channel\n   376\t  reader and one socket may serve several attachments, and delivers only a\n   377\t  complete message. Loss of any part is loss of the whole message,\n   378\t  recovered by the link's resend rule. Reassembly is bounded by two\n   379\t  composition data, `:dao.stream.udp/max-message-bytes` (default 64 KiB)\n   380\t  and `:dao.stream.udp/max-partial-messages`, evicting the oldest partial\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
